From 3aeeb80b65a84be29a733cefa31a6d3f27d2a49f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ALAS Headless Research <local@alas-headless.invalid>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add an Android window contract to the NULL backend

The upstream NULL backend is a test renderer: it ignores the native window,
reports a hard-coded 100x100 surface, returns from swap immediately, and fills
readback bytes with a non-zero sentinel.  Those semantics are useful to ANGLE
tests but insufficient for an Android Unity player.

For Android NULL-only builds this patch:

* validates and retains the ANativeWindow;
* reports its logical size and posts one zero-filled RGBA compositor buffer;
* paces eglSwapBuffers using a synthetic refresh rate;
* implements basic sync-control counters; and
* makes direct/PBO readback deterministically zero-filled.

The synthetic refresh rate defaults to 60 Hz and can be changed on a custom
Android image with debug.angle.null_refresh_hz.  Renderer and vendor strings
remain honestly reported as NULL.
